            <ArticleTitle>Surgery for angina pectoris: a historical perspective.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery disease continues to be the major cause of death in the United States each year with close to 1 million people dying of this disease annually, one third of those being under the age of 65. An estimated 5 million people in this country suffer some degree of disability from angina pectoris.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
